✨ Features
🤖 AI-powered feedback analysis
🧠 Automatic feedback categorization
📝 User feedback collected through an n8n form
🔀 Smart routing using a Switch node
🗃️ Automatic storage in Airtable
💬 Real-time notifications in Slack
📧 Email notifications using Gmail
🔄 Original form data preserved using the Merge node
🛠️ Technologies Used
n8n – Workflow automation
Google Gemini AI – AI analysis and categorization
Airtable – Feedback data storage
Slack – Team notifications
Gmail – Email notifications
n8n Form Trigger – User feedback collection
🔄 Workflow Explanation
1. On Form Submission

The workflow starts when a user submits feedback through the n8n form.

The form submission may contain information such as:

User feedback
User name
Email address
Feedback details

The submitted data is then passed to the AI Agent.

2. AI Agent

The AI Agent analyzes the submitted feedback and determines its category.

The AI Agent is connected to:

Google Gemini Chat Model
Structured Output Parser

The AI model processes the feedback and returns structured data that can be used by the rest of the workflow.


3. Merge Node

The Merge node combines:

Original form submission data
AI-generated analysis

This ensures that the workflow keeps both the user's original feedback and the AI categorization.

4. Switch Node

The Switch node routes the feedback depending on the category generated by the AI Agent.

Current categories include:

Complaint
Feature Request

Each category follows a different automation path.

😠 Complaint Workflow

When feedback is categorized as a Complaint:

Complaint
    ↓
Airtable
    ↓
Slack
    ↓
Gmail
Airtable

The complaint is automatically stored in Airtable.

This creates a centralized database where the team can review and manage complaints.

Slack

A Slack notification is sent to inform the team about the complaint.

This allows the team to respond quickly to important user issues.

Gmail

An email notification is sent after the complaint has been processed.

💡 Feature Request Workflow

When feedback is categorized as a Feature Request:

Feature Request
      ↓
   Airtable
      ↓
    Slack

The feature request is:

Stored in Airtable.
Sent to the team through Slack.

This helps the team maintain a structured list of user-requested features.

📊 Example Workflow
User submits feedback:

"The application is difficult to use on mobile devices."

        ↓

AI Agent analyzes feedback

        ↓

Category: Complaint

        ↓

Store complaint in Airtable

        ↓

Send notification to Slack

        ↓

Send email notification

Another example:

User submits feedback:

"It would be great if the application had dark mode."

        ↓

AI Agent analyzes feedback

        ↓

Category: Feature Request

        ↓

Store request in Airtable

        ↓

Send notification to Slack
📦 Required Credentials

Before using this workflow, configure the following credentials in n8n:

Google Gemini

Used by the AI Agent for analyzing and categorizing feedback.

Airtable

Used to store:

Complaints
Feature requests
User feedback
AI-generated summaries
Slack

Used to send real-time notifications to the team.

Gmail

Used to send email notifications for complaint-related feedback.

⚙️ How to Use
1. Import the workflow

Download the workflow JSON file and import it into n8n.

2. Configure credentials

Add your credentials for:

Google Gemini
Airtable
Slack
Gmail
3. Configure the AI Agent

Set up the AI Agent with instructions to:

Analyze incoming feedback.
Determine the appropriate category.
Return structured output.
4. Configure Airtable

Create the required tables and fields for storing:

User feedback
Category
AI summary
Submission information
5. Configure Slack and Gmail

Update the destination channels and email settings according to your requirements.

6. Activate the workflow

Once everything is configured, activate the workflow.

New form submissions will then be processed automatically.

